  "report": {
    "title": "Markdown List Auto-Completion Adds Symbol to Current Line Instead of New Line",
    "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nWhen using the Markdown editor in the content management system, the auto-completion feature for unordered lists is behaving incorrectly. When entering `- 123` or `* 123` and pressing Enter, the system appends an extra `-` or `*` to the end of the current line instead of inserting it on a new line.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open the Markdown editor in the content publishing interface.\n2. Type `- 123` (or `* 123`) in the editor.\n3. Press the Enter key to create a new line.\n\n## Expected Behavior\n- The current line should remain as `- 123` (or `* 123`).\n- A new line should be automatically prepended with `-` (or `*`) to continue the unordered list.\n\n## Actual Behavior\n- The current line becomes `- 123-` (or `* 123*`) after pressing Enter.\n- The line break is not properly applied, and the list symbol is incorrectly appended to the existing line.\n\n### The version of Memos you're using\n\n\n0.25.2\n\n### Screenshots or additional context\n\n<img width=\"740\" height=\"145\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/eca12494-ff3d-47cf-8392-2eb1dbba1302\" />",
    "source_url": "https://github.com/usememos/memos/issues/5236",
    "repo": null,
    "number": 5236
  },
  "app_url": "http://localhost:16203",
  "app_label": "Memos, a self-hosted note-taking app",
